IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cbca-core-definitions`
IMPORT `cb4-common`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part XVIII, ss 226 to 228: AFTER DISSOLUTION.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Department of Justice Canada consolidation
-- current to 2026-09-30; not verified against the official text.
--
-- WHAT THIS MODULE IS. A dissolved corporation can still be sued (for two years), its property is still
-- there to satisfy a judgment, and shareholders who received its property can be made to give it back, up to
-- what they received (s 226). The share of an unfindable creditor or shareholder goes to the Receiver General
-- (s 227). Property that nobody has disposed of vests in the Crown, and goes back to a revived corporation
-- (s 228).
--
-- "Within two years after its dissolution" (ss 226(2)(b), 226(4)) counts from the date of dissolution, which
-- is the date shown in the certificate of dissolution: that day is day 0 and the last day is the same day two
-- years on (keel fork F1). Section 106 and 113 (notices), 209 (revival) and the Canada Corporations Act
-- (1970) are not part of this module. "Her Majesty" is as the text has it.

§§ `s 226 Continuation of actions; service; reimbursement`

-- (1): "includes": a listed person is a shareholder for s 226 (JUST TRUE); anyone else is not decided.
-- src:2829 | Definition of shareholder
-- src:2830 | 226 (1) In this section, shareholder includes the heirs and personal representatives of a shareholder.
@ref CBCA s 226(1) (src:2830)
DECLARE `Kind of person for the word shareholder in s 226(1)` IS ONE OF
    `a shareholder, for the word shareholder in s 226(1)`
    `an heir of a shareholder`
    `a personal representative of a shareholder`
    `a person who is not a shareholder, an heir or a personal representative (s 226(1))`

@ref CBCA s 226(1) (src:2830)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of person for the word shareholder in s 226(1)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`whether a person is a shareholder within s 226(1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a person who is not a shareholder, an heir or a personal representative (s 226(1))` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:2831 | Continuation of actions
-- src:2832 | (2) Notwithstanding the dissolution of a body corporate under this Act,
-- src:2833 | (a) a civil, criminal or administrative action or proceeding commenced by or against the body corporate before its dissolution may be continued as if the body corporate had not been dissolved;
-- src:2834 | (b) a civil, criminal or administrative action or proceeding may be brought against the body corporate within two years after its dissolution as if the body corporate had not been dissolved; and
-- src:2835 | (c) any property that would have been available to satisfy any judgment or order if the body corporate had not been dissolved remains available for such purpose.
@ref CBCA s 226(2)(a) (src:2832-2833)
GIVEN `the body corporate has been dissolved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action or proceeding was commenced by or against the body corporate before its dissolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the action may be continued as if the body corporate had not been dissolved within s 226(2)(a)` MEANS
        `the body corporate has been dissolved`
    AND `the action or proceeding was commenced by or against the body corporate before its dissolution`

@ref CBCA s 226(2)(b) (src:2832 src:2834)
GIVEN `the date of dissolution` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for an action to be brought against the dissolved body corporate within s 226(2)(b)` MEANS
    `the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 2, `unit of time` IS `calendar years`) `counted from` `the date of dissolution`

@ref CBCA s 226(2)(b) (src:2832 src:2834)
GIVEN `the date of dissolution` IS A DATE
      `the day the action was brought` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the action may be brought against the dissolved body corporate within s 226(2)(b)` MEANS
    `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 2, `unit of time` IS `calendar years`) `the date of dissolution` `the day the action was brought`

@ref CBCA s 226(2)(c) (src:2832 src:2835)
GIVEN `the body corporate has been dissolved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property would have been available to satisfy the judgment or order if the body corporate had not been dissolved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the property remains available to satisfy the judgment or order within s 226(2)(c)` MEANS
        `the body corporate has been dissolved`
    AND `the property would have been available to satisfy the judgment or order if the body corporate had not been dissolved`

-- (3) and (3.1) say service MAY be effected on the named persons. They do not say that service on anyone else
-- is bad, so a person who is not named gets NOTHING, not FALSE.
-- src:2836 | Service
-- src:2837 | (3) Service of a document on a corporation after its dissolution may be effected by serving the document on a person shown in the last notice filed under section 106 or 113.
@ref CBCA s 226(3) (src:2837)
GIVEN `the person served is shown in the last notice filed under section 106 or 113` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`whether service on a dissolved corporation is effected by serving this person within s 226(3)` MEANS
    IF `the person served is shown in the last notice filed under section 106 or 113`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2838 | Idem
-- src:2839 | (3.1) Service of a document on a company to which the Canada Corporations Act, chapter C-32 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, applied that has been dissolved by subsection 261(8) of the Canada Business Corporations Act, chapter 33 of the Statutes of Canada, 1974-75-76 and chapter 9 of the Statutes of Canada, 1978-79, may be effected by serving the document on a person shown as a director in the last annual summary filed by the company pursuant to the Canada Corporations Act.
@ref CBCA s 226(3.1) (src:2839)
GIVEN `the company was one to which the Canada Corporations Act, chapter C-32 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, applied and was dissolved by subsection 261(8) of the Canada Business Corporations Act, chapter 33 of the Statutes of Canada, 1974-75-76` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person served is shown as a director in the last annual summary filed by the company under the Canada Corporations Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`whether service on a company dissolved by subsection 261(8) is effected by serving this person within s 226(3.1)` MEANS
    IF     `the company was one to which the Canada Corporations Act, chapter C-32 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, applied and was dissolved by subsection 261(8) of the Canada Business Corporations Act, chapter 33 of the Statutes of Canada, 1974-75-76`
       AND `the person served is shown as a director in the last annual summary filed by the company under the Canada Corporations Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (4): liable "to the extent of the amount received": the least of what is claimed and what was received.
-- src:2840 | Reimbursement
-- src:2841 | (4) Notwithstanding the dissolution of a body corporate under this Act, a shareholder to whom any of its property has been distributed is liable to any person claiming under subsection (2) to the extent of the amount received by that shareholder on such distribution, and an action to enforce such liability may be brought within two years after the date of the dissolution of the body corporate.
@ref CBCA s 226(4) (src:2841)
GIVEN `a shareholder received property of the body corporate on a distribution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is claiming under subsection 226(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount the claimant is owed` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount received by the shareholder on the distribution` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most the shareholder is liable to pay within s 226(4)` MEANS
    IF     `a shareholder received property of the body corporate on a distribution`
       AND `the person is claiming under subsection 226(2)`
    THEN (IF `the amount the claimant is owed` LESS THAN `the amount received by the shareholder on the distribution`
          THEN `the amount the claimant is owed`
          ELSE `the amount received by the shareholder on the distribution`)
    ELSE 0

@ref CBCA s 226(4) (src:2841)
GIVEN `the date of dissolution` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for an action against a shareholder to be brought within s 226(4)` MEANS
    `the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 2, `unit of time` IS `calendar years`) `counted from` `the date of dissolution`

@ref CBCA s 226(4) (src:2841)
GIVEN `the date of dissolution` IS A DATE
      `the day the action was brought` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the action against a shareholder is brought in time within s 226(4)` MEANS
    `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 2, `unit of time` IS `calendar years`) `the date of dissolution` `the day the action was brought`

-- src:2842 | Representative action
-- src:2843 | (5) A court may order an action referred to in subsection (4) to be brought against the persons who were shareholders as a class, subject to such conditions as the court thinks fit and, if the plaintiff establishes a claim, the court may refer the proceedings to a referee or other officer of the court who may
-- src:2844 | (a) add as a party to the proceedings each person who was a shareholder found by the plaintiff;
-- src:2845 | (b) determine, subject to subsection (4), the amount that each person who was a shareholder shall contribute towards satisfaction of the plaintiff’s claim; and
-- src:2846 | (c) direct payment of the amounts so determined.
@ref CBCA s 226(5) (src:2843)
GIVEN `an action is referred to in subsection 226(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a court may order the action to be brought against the former shareholders as a class within s 226(5)` MEANS
    `an action is referred to in subsection 226(4)`

@ref CBCA s 226(5)(a) (src:2843-2844)
GIVEN `the plaintiff has established a claim in an action brought against the former shareholders as a class` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the referee may add as a party each former shareholder found by the plaintiff within s 226(5)(a)` MEANS
    `the plaintiff has established a claim in an action brought against the former shareholders as a class`

@ref CBCA s 226(5)(b) (src:2843 src:2845)
GIVEN `the plaintiff has established a claim in an action brought against the former shareholders as a class` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount the former shareholder received on the distribution` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount the referee proposes the former shareholder contribute` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the referee may require this contribution within s 226(5)(b)` MEANS
        `the plaintiff has established a claim in an action brought against the former shareholders as a class`
    AND `the amount the referee proposes the former shareholder contribute` AT MOST `the amount the former shareholder received on the distribution`

@ref CBCA s 226(5)(c) (src:2843 src:2846)
GIVEN `the referee has determined the amounts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the referee may direct payment of the amounts determined within s 226(5)(c)` MEANS
    `the referee has determined the amounts`

§§ `s 227 Unknown claimants`

-- src:2847 | Unknown claimants
-- src:2848 | 227 (1) On the dissolution of a body corporate under this Act, the portion of the property distributable to a creditor or shareholder who cannot be found shall be converted into money and paid to the Receiver General.
@ref CBCA s 227(1) (src:2848)
GIVEN `the body corporate has been dissolved under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the creditor or shareholder cannot be found` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the portion must be converted into money and paid to the Receiver General within s 227(1)` MEANS
        `the body corporate has been dissolved under this Act`
    AND `the creditor or shareholder cannot be found`

-- src:2849 | Constructive satisfaction
-- src:2850 | (2) A payment under subsection (1) is deemed to be in satisfaction of a debt or claim of such creditor or shareholder.
@ref CBCA s 227(2) (src:2850)
GIVEN `a payment has been made under subsection 227(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the payment is deemed to satisfy the debt or claim within s 227(2)` MEANS
    `a payment has been made under subsection 227(1)`

-- src:2851 | Recovery
-- src:2852 | (3) A person who establishes an entitlement to any moneys paid to the Receiver General under this Act shall be paid by the Receiver General an equivalent amount out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund.
@ref CBCA s 227(3) (src:2852)
GIVEN `the person establishes an entitlement to moneys paid to the Receiver General under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Receiver General must pay the person out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund within s 227(3)` MEANS
    `the person establishes an entitlement to moneys paid to the Receiver General under this Act`

@ref CBCA s 227(3) (src:2852)
GIVEN `the moneys paid to the Receiver General to which the person is entitled` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount the Receiver General pays within s 227(3)` MEANS
    `the moneys paid to the Receiver General to which the person is entitled`

§§ `s 228 Vesting in the Crown; return on revival`

-- (1): subject to s 226(2) and s 227, undisposed property vests in Her Majesty in right of Canada.
-- src:2853 | Vesting in Crown
-- src:2854 | 228 (1) Subject to subsection 226(2) and section 227, property of a body corporate that has not been disposed of at the date of its dissolution under this Act vests in Her Majesty in right of Canada.
@ref CBCA s 228(1) (src:2854)
GIVEN `the body corporate has been dissolved under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property had not been disposed of at the date of dissolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property remains available under subsection 226(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property is the portion within section 227` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the property vests in Her Majesty in right of Canada within s 228(1)` MEANS
        `the body corporate has been dissolved under this Act`
    AND `the property had not been disposed of at the date of dissolution`
    AND (NOT `the property remains available under subsection 226(2)`)
    AND (NOT `the property is the portion within section 227`)

-- src:2855 | Return of property on revival
-- src:2856 | (2) If a body corporate is revived as a corporation under section 209, any property, other than money, that vested in Her Majesty pursuant to subsection (1), that has not been disposed of shall be returned to the corporation and there shall be paid to the corporation out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund
@ref CBCA s 228(2) (src:2856)
GIVEN `the body corporate is revived as a corporation under section 209` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property is not money` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property vested in Her Majesty under subsection 228(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property has not been disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the property is returned to the corporation within s 228(2)` MEANS
        `the body corporate is revived as a corporation under section 209`
    AND `the property is not money`
    AND `the property vested in Her Majesty under subsection 228(1)`
    AND `the property has not been disposed of`

-- src:2857 | (a) an amount equal to any money received by Her Majesty pursuant to subsection (1); and
@ref CBCA s 228(2)(a) (src:2857)
GIVEN `the body corporate is revived as a corporation under section 209` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the money received by Her Majesty under subsection 228(1)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount paid to the corporation under s 228(2)(a)` MEANS
    IF `the body corporate is revived as a corporation under section 209`
    THEN `the money received by Her Majesty under subsection 228(1)`
    ELSE 0

-- src:2858 | (b) where property other than money vested in Her Majesty pursuant to subsection (1) and that property has been disposed of, an amount equal to the lesser of
-- src:2859 | (i) the value of any such property at the date it vested in Her Majesty, and
-- src:2860 | (ii) the amount realized by Her Majesty from the disposition of that property.
@ref CBCA s 228(2)(b) (src:2858-2860)
GIVEN `the body corporate is revived as a corporation under section 209` IS A BOOLEAN
      `property other than money vested in Her Majesty under subsection 228(1) and has been disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the property at the date it vested` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount realized by Her Majesty from the disposition` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount paid to the corporation under s 228(2)(b)` MEANS
    IF     `the body corporate is revived as a corporation under section 209`
       AND `property other than money vested in Her Majesty under subsection 228(1) and has been disposed of`
    THEN (IF `the value of the property at the date it vested` LESS THAN `the amount realized by Her Majesty from the disposition`
          THEN `the value of the property at the date it vested`
          ELSE `the amount realized by Her Majesty from the disposition`)
    ELSE 0
